Patches in this folder are applied on top of the live data pulled from the
private data repo, before the neoradar-cli conversion runs.

Layout: anything under diffs/**/*.patch is applied (sorted by path).
Suggested grouping:
  diffs/sector_files/*.patch  - against the SCT / SCT2 / ESE
  diffs/icao_data/*.patch     - against ICAO_Aircraft.txt / ICAO_Airlines.txt
  diffs/euroscope_data/*.patch

Authoring a patch:

1. Run the workflow's sync step locally (or copy the live SCT/ESE/ICAO into
   sector_files/ and icao_data/). Those files are .gitignored so git won't
   pick them up directly.

2. Edit the file in place.

3. Generate a patch with paths relative to the repo root:

     git diff --no-index --relative \
       sector_files/Original.sct sector_files/Original.sct \
       > diffs/sector_files/fix-something.patch

   Or, if the file is temporarily un-ignored:

     git diff sector_files/Original.sct > diffs/sector_files/fix-something.patch

4. Commit the .patch file. The CI step applies it with:

     git apply --whitespace=fix <patch>

Keep one logical change per patch so PRs stay reviewable.
